    <string name="calib_title">Arrow direction</string>
    <string name="calib_help">Turn the phone slowly through a full circle, or turn the whole car. The ring fills as you go. That is what calibrates a compass: the sensor watches the magnetic field sweep past and works out how much the car\'s bodywork is bending it.\n\nWhen the ring is full, check the arrow against a road you can see on the map. If it is off, nudge it, then press Done.</string>
    <string name="calib_nudge">Turn the arrow</string>
    <string name="calib_l90">90° left</string>
    <string name="calib_l5">5° left</string>
    <string name="calib_r5">5° right</string>
    <string name="calib_r90">90° right</string>
    <string name="calib_flip">Turn it right round (180°)</string>
    <string name="calib_save">Save</string>
    <string name="calib_reset">Forget</string>
    <string name="calib_note">Standing still the arrow is a compass, so you know which way you are facing before you set off. As soon as the car is moving it switches to GPS, which measures the direction of travel from orbit and cannot be bent by the car\'s bodywork; the compass comes back a few seconds after you stop. Readings taken in a distorted magnetic field are thrown away rather than shown.</string>
    <string name="calib_button">Calibrate arrow direction</string>
    <string name="calib_no_sensor">This device has no compass, so the arrow can only get its direction from GPS once you start driving.</string>
    <string name="calib_learned">Learned automatically while driving: offset %1$d°</string>
    <string name="calib_manual">Set by hand: offset %1$d°</string>
    <string name="calib_none">Not calibrated yet. Drive above 25 km/h and it sorts itself out.</string>
    <string name="calib_readout_sub">phone compass %1$d° · using the %2$s</string>
    <string name="calib_axis_top">top edge of the phone</string>
    <string name="calib_axis_screen">way the screen faces</string>
    <string name="calib_progress">%1$d%% of the circle covered</string>
    <string name="calib_turn_more">Keep turning. The ring fills as the compass sees each direction.</string>
    <string name="calib_turned_enough">Full circle covered. Offset %1$d°. Check the arrow against the road, then press Done.</string>
    <string name="calib_ready">Compass reports itself accurate. Offset %1$d°. Press Done.</string>
    <string name="calib_done">Done</string>
